    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d870">

                <pb facs="0844" n="832" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg832"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Moose, James/439: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-18T10:00:00+03:06">July 18, 1943—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:41 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. Reference is made to the Department’s instruction of June 10 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">14</hi>], 1943.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d870-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Kirk’s letter of recall and my letter of credence were presented to Amir Faisal
                    as Viceroy<anchor n="7" xml:id="d870-f2"/> today. Forms executed.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Cairo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d870-f1" n="6" xml:id="d870-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d870-f2" n="7" xml:id="d870-f2-content">
                <p>The Amir, a son of King Ibn Sand, was also Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
